      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__edge__getters_1ga86b1645777ad4829da99a395a3b42157" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>const int</type>
        <definition>const int ndxlGetEdgeChannels</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLEdge *_Edge, NDXLChannel **_Channels)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlGetEdgeChannels</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1aa30ac2f40da4dbe7d841088a78f957fe" kindref="member">NDXLEdge</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Edge</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1a40b73c1a687ab1376515b42d4294c079" kindref="member">NDXLChannel</ref> **</type>
          <declname>_Channels</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Gets a list of all the noise channels affecting an edge. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Edge</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target edge to retrieve the noise channels of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">_Channels</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to a user-allocated array of <ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1a40b73c1a687ab1376515b42d4294c079" kindref="member">NDXLChannel</ref> pointers. The array must contain at least ndxlGetEdgeChannelCount(_Edge) elements. The function populates the array in-place.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If either _Edge or _Channels are NULL, returns <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>, otherwise populates _Channels with the noise channel pointers associated with _Edge, and returns NDXL_OK.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The caller retains ownership of the array, but not of the <ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1a40b73c1a687ab1376515b42d4294c079" kindref="member">NDXLChannel</ref> objects referenced by its elements. These pointers refer to the original objects in the owning network of _Edge, so modifications through them affect those objects directly. The returned list can be used to modify or destroy its referenced objects without invalidating the array itself.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>The function does not verify the capacity of the supplied array. Providing an inadequately sized array can result in out-of-bounds writes and undefined behaviour.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Errors raised</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Edge is NULL.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Channels is NULL.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__edge__getters_1ga9a94b25401f370a604ba1131ab87995f" kindref="member">ndxlGetEdgeChannelCount</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
