        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Gets the time-delayed and directed state vector of an edge as seen by one of its vertices. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Edge</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target edge to retrieve the relative state of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Vertex</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The vertex from whose perspective the edge state vector is evaluated.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If either _Edge or _Vertex are NULL, or _Edge is not connected to _Vertex, returns NULL, otherwise returns the delayed and directed state vector of the edge as seen by _Vertex.<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>If _Edge is directed and _Vertex is the <computeroutput>source</computeroutput> vertex of _Edge, always returns the zero-vector of the edge regardless of the delay.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If _Edge is delayed, returns the zero-vector of the edge for t &lt; delay, and the current state vector for t greater than or equal to delay.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If _Edge is neither directed nor delayed, returns the current state vector of _Edge.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>If and only if both the delay of _Edge is zero and it is undirected, is this equivalent to calling ndxlEdgeState(_Edge).</para>
</simplesect>
